  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) is a cloud computing service model in which a provider delivers virtualised computing resources \u2014 including virtual machines, storage, networking, and bare-metal servers \u2014 over the internet on a pay-per-use basis, while the customer manages the operating system, middleware, and applications. IaaS abstracts away physical hardware procurement and data centre operations, enabling organisations to provision and de-provision compute capacity elastically. Major IaaS providers include Amazon Web Services (EC2/S3), Microsoft Azure (Virtual Machines), and Google Cloud Platform (Compute Engine).",
